  "introTitle1": "What is a restoration plan?",
  "introBody1": "Every monsoon, rain washes soil off hills and fields into the lake. A plan picks where to build simple soil-saving works, and JalRakshak shows how much soil would stay on the land instead.",
  "introTitle2": "Three fixes",
  "introBody2": "Contour bunds: low earth walls along the slope of farm fields that slow water down.\n\nContour trenches: shallow trenches dug along hill slopes that catch running water.\n\nRevegetation: grass and shrubs on bare hills whose roots hold the soil. Takes 2–3 seasons.",
  "introTitle3": "Where the numbers come from",
  "introBody3": "Satellite data on rainfall, soil, slope and plant cover feeds a standard soil-erosion model (RUSLE). Each fix changes how fast water runs off. The results are estimates to compare places, not measurements.",
  "introTitle4": "Start where it matters most",
  "introBody4": "Begin with the zones that lose the most soil. Gram panchayats can fund these works under MGNREGA. Tap any zone to see why it erodes and what to do.",
  "introNext": "Next",
  "introSkip": "Skip",
  "introStart": "Start planning",

